# models.py audit

- [ ] Are all input objects validated with exact-key, fail-closed semantics?
- [ ] Are event IDs and sequence indexes unique and canonical?
- [ ] Does every edge point strictly from an earlier occurrence to a later occurrence?
- [ ] Are occurrence identity and canonical mathematical-state identity kept separate?
- [ ] Are non-finite JSON values and bool-as-int inputs rejected?
- [ ] Does adding or changing an enum require a schema-version decision?

